WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.860
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.990
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.240
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.790
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.290
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.140
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.100
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.330
You've gotten better, Tsuda.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.120
This is surprising!

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.500
So the whole crew has been replaced.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:01.300
I want this man detained, and locked in the ship's hold.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.020
With a radar that far surpasses yours...

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.020
...and anti-ship weapons with a shooting range...

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.980
...of 110 thousand yards...

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.150
...even before your forces start to move,

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.150
they will have sunk this ship.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:22.240
Deadline

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.330
That's just impossible!

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.710
It's just a childish threat, Lieutenant!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.960
There's no way they would attack...

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.880
...a tanker full of supplies for them!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.840
So you intend to go down with me.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.800
I'm the only person who knows the code to halt the attack!

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.890
You'll all sink to the bottom with me!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.680
Is that the truth, Lieutenant?

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.020
I know as much as you do.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.770
But then, it would be appropriate...

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.650
...judging by how confidential everything's been.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.070
Commander Kadomatsu described...

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.780
...the Mirai's capabilities very accurately.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.870
Although it's hard to believe,

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.870
they have a missile with a firing range of 55 miles.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.830
I saw it with my own eyes.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.960
Time to the 20 mile line?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.880
Less than 15 minutes!

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.050
That can't be! We're supposed to be in control here.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.470
Yet we're left with only 3 options?!

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.260
We can assume that it's a bluff,

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.810
ignore the empty threat, and continue ahead with this ship.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.890
We can choose to believe what this man has said...

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.770
...and let him use the secret code to halt the assault.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.400
Or we can stop at the 20 mile line

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.690
and await the arrival of our attack force.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.950
I'm sure you've realized that this is a trade-off.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.910
I have some conditions of my own!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.080
What?!

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.370
There are two conditions to halt the attack.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.910
First, your ship is not to interfere with the re-supply of our ship...

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.380
...and our lives on our ship must be assured and confirmed.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.130
Secondly, you are to remain unarmed!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.130
What?!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.840
If you don't comply with these terms...

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.760
...this ship will be sunk in no time!

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.520
I see. You're an excellent soldier too.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.570
Take him to the communications room!

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.120
Only 550 more until we pass the 20 mile line.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.000
Listen! They will only radio us once!

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.210
Don't miss it!

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.960
Got it!

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.250
I've never heard such a strong signal output!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.960
The signal's so strong!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.150
The current sea route is sealed off.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.860
Change your course right now.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.780
What's the code to halt the attack?

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.700
I'd like my pistol back first.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:08.910
Lieutenant, you mustn't!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.620
The ship ahead of us is not armed.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.630
And the secret code didn't exist in the first place!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.550
Why would a ship that's ready for battle

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.340
even bother to send a radio message out?!

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.090
We are very different from you.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:32.520
What happens if this ship doesn't respond correctly?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.640
The Japanese of the future...

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.440
...won't just write off a civilian ship...

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.400
...as collateral damage.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.860
The Japanese of the future?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.440
You're still spouting that nonsense?!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.610
Even if you don't believe me, the truth will not change.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:50.950
Tsuda.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.620
You must stay calm.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.870
Commander Kadomatsu wants the supplies,

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.830
and you want to investigate that ship.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.170
Don't be restricted by your emotions,

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.630
or let them narrow your view of the issues at hand.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.470
You need to prioritize and focus on what's important.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:10.890
Backing down now is a strategy in itself, and not a defeat.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.510
After you've finished loading, how about granting...

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:16.600
...Lieutenant Tsuda a tour of Mirai?

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.100
What's that?!

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.360
That's fifty-fifty right? I think it's a fair deal.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.120
It's decided then, Commander Kadomatsu?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.330
The code to halt the attack.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.880
Message from Approaching Target Alpha!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.380
What does it say?

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.850
The opening ceremony of the Tokyo Olympics...

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.390
...was a fine and cloudy day.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.720
So cloudy was included?

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.600
No mistake about it?

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.600
They repeated it twice. It's confirmed.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.610
That means the acquisition was successful.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.440
Cloudy would mean... I'm afraid...

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.740
this message might be a warning...

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.400
...that someone may be interrupting our main plan.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.290
We've passed the 20 mile line!

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.920
Understanding has prevented a fight.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.670
Attacks from both sides have been halted.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:29.920
For now,

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.090
a compromise has settled things.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.020
Tanker Sighted! 150 degrees!

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.320
It's our supplies!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.660
Another 2000 to destination!

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.870
Cruiser Type Vessel Sighted!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.540
Quite a change of events.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.540
Were you expecting this all along?

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.460
Not at all.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.210
I didn't see that impressive bluff coming.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.220
Both sides to stop!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.840
Target in front of ship...

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.800
...passed distance of 1500.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.680
Officer Kawamoto, what do you think about this?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.220
Well, Lieutenant...

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.480
Regarding the story about 60 years ahead of our time,

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.400
I don't understand it one bit.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:29.280
It's definitely a ship I've never seen before but obviously it's a warship.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:34.280
I was certain that he was lying till I saw this ship.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.620
This ship is bigger than the Takao!

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.620
But it looks very clean and tidy.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.500
Hey, look at that mast!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.080
It'd topple in a hurricane for sure!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.000
It's supposed to be a cruiser but it's only got one cannon?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.210
How's it gonna fight with that?

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.760
I heard something strange about it!

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:59.680
Someone said that cruiser's not from this era!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.730
What's that about?

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.570
They all look like they've seen a ghost!

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.150
I don't see anyone in a soldier's uniform.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.150
They all seem to be sailors.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.860
There's a good chance that they're all in disguise.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.120
Commander Kadomatsu's on the bridge!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.620
And Lieutenant Kusaka's with him!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.710
So that's what "fine and cloudy" means.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.290
A ranking navy officer's been sighted.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.960
Captain, that means that all those men...

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.930
Yes. They're all soldiers.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.220
Flag signals from the Tanker!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.300
Approaching ship from Port side!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.970
Request authorization!

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.850
A 10 thousand ton tanker...

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.810
...without tug boats,

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:50.020
approaching at low speed despite poor maneuverability.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.730
They must be very confident of their skills.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:56.990
Tanker closing in on side! Port side prepare to moor!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.070
Port side prepare to moor!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.370
Lock main cannon onto tanker!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.040
Cannon?!

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.920
What are those fellas thinking?!

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:16.340
We're all members of the Navy! Why point the cannon at us?!

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.840
Hey, look at that!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.180
The Navy soldiers are all wearing iron helmets...

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.180
...like the German Soldiers?!

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.970
And they aren't carrying T-38s either.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:29.190
Those guys aren't from the Navy!

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:31.480
All units and crew stand by!

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.940
Throw the rope over!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.110
Wind Number One!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.530
Rope for number three!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.800
I must say they've done pretty well without a tug boat!

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.630
Mooring Operation Complete!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.510
I'll go get permission to board ship.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.520
Sorry, but you'll have to play hostage.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.900
Do you think I'm still qualified to be a hostage?

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.270
Yes I do.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.070
What about Lieutenant Tsuda?

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.740
Please place yourself in my custody for now.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.070
Well it seems like I've been accepted.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.000
Welcome back, Commander!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.170
Good job protecting this ship.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.140
What's wrong? Did something happen?

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:47.600
No, just glad to see you, sir.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.230
I was hoping you'd bring a few Malayan Beauties back with you

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.230
but you've brought something more.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.320
We need to talk. Bring the Weapons Officer too.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.070
There's no need for that.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:04.320
This ship is still controlled by its captain.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:08.200
I got it.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.540
Commander Kadomatsu, reporting for duty!

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.260
I'd like to put this back in your care.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.550
Fortunately, there was no need to use it.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.600
That's good to hear. Well done.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.770
And you observed the era carefully?

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.100
Yes!

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:38.610
Look at their sunken eyes and serious faces!

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:41.150
Those are the faces of soldiers.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.860
Although I was mentally prepared...

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:46.990
...I didn't intend to alter history so much.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.030
I'm very sorry about this!

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:51.500
Oh no, this isn't your fault.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:57.250
I understand that Kusaka mentioned Guadalcanal?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:03.340
Humans can be a little more troublesome than ships.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:09.010
We can't just hammer a pin in and stop where we are.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.970
Either we leave it to fate, and go along with the flow...

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.890
...or we fight against the current.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.360
People aren't strong enough to just sail on...

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.190
...without a destination.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.570
Captain, it is very hard to live a life without...

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.530
...something to protect.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.660
What I saw on land wasn't just history itself,

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.200
but also the people living in this era.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:38.000
It didn't matter whether they were Japanese or Asians.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:44.090
Maybe we should be putting our strengths to better use.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.510
For the sake of those people who cross our paths...

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.800
...and for our own sake as well.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.440
Permission granted for boarding.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.440
Only for Lieutenant Tsuda, however.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:08.200
You are to obey orders while on board and remain unarmed.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.370
No other exceptions will be allowed.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:15.330
What?! Lieutenant! It's too dangerous to go alone!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.120
Let's make preparations for assault.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:25.010
Thank you for the permission. I accept all terms!

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.060
I am the captain, Umezu.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.980
Navy Lieutenant, Kazuma Tsuda.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.740
You're very young. When were you born?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.200
In the Taisho period Second Year.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.710
That's the same year as my father.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.170
Welcome aboard our ship, Mirai!

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.050
Thank you!

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:28.650
Here you go.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:39.790
This is the crew canteen. We've been having canned food...

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.790
...for the past few days, and everyone's getting sick of it.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:43.750
That's a TV Monitor.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.840
It's similar to the On Board screenings you have.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.260
We've been watching the same stuff over and over.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.300
We watched on even though we've memorized the lines.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:57.930
Up ahead is the medical room.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.610
This ship has women on board too?

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:08.610
Oh, you mean female officers?

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:12.150
Well, I guess it's uncommon for them to be on SDF ships.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.740
It'll be hard for you to believe...

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:17.240
...but female pilots are no longer rarities.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:22.410
Heisei 13th Year, Inspection Complete.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.960
Heisei?!

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:35.390
Clear the deck now! Unloading the rice!

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.550
Okay here!

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:42.680
They're speaking Japanese but, with western accents.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.850
Isn't this Thai rice? I don't mind old rice...

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.610
...but give me Koshi Hikari!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.360
Stop complaining.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:52.530
Koshi Hikari doesn't exist in the Showa 17th Year!

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:02.450
How was it?

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.170
Does it feel real after seeing it yourself?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:10.000
Yes, though I'm still confused.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.920
I have no idea how I should be approaching this matter.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.300
And the data room?

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.390
Yes. They brought me there.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:24.230
Did you see it? The transition of this war?

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:32.230
Ever since cadet school, and even after I was given a post...

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:35.110
I always aspired to be like you and worked hard to be strong

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.490
and to execute wartime strategies...

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:38.820
...with composure.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.750
Inside this room are records of the fate of Imperial Japan...

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.250
...and millions of people's lives...

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:56.720
...and the outcome of this battle.

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.100
I couldn't find the courage to do it!

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.320
The cruelty of war calls for strength of mind...

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.320
...and the power to believe!

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.570
If I were to know everything, and still be expected to...

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:19.280
...send my men out knowing they would die...

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.580
I don't think I could do something like that!

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.000
This is a drink from America.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.620
It was surprising enough for me to see this come out of...

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:31.380
...an unmanned machine, but more to find it on a Japanese ship!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:36.550
Just how am I supposed to explain this to my superiors?

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:39.800
You're well aware of the situation.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:43.640
There will come a time when Japan will need such things.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:48.560
The Allied forces are on their way to Truk Island, right?

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:52.980
Yes. They are preparing for the next operation.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:54.980
So you've seen them too?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:57.940
The two auto gyros in the back of the rear hangar.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.990
A fighter plane and a big patrol plane.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.660
I heard that they both have a flight range of 370 miles.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.580
After Mirai finishes loading supplies,

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.580
I'm guessing that it will head for the waters of Guadalcanal.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.170
If we travel the sea route with that auto-gyro...

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.130
Fly to Truk on that Auto-gyro?

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.720
Commander-in-Chief Yamamoto aside, the only thing that's...

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.680
...capable of changing the minds of the pro-war lobbyists...

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:30.890
...isn't words, but the future in front of us.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.910
Attention. This is Captain Umezu.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:46.990
I thank everyone for ensuring the success of the resupply.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:52.420
Tomorrow morning, this ship will leave for a new operation.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:55.040
The operation area is...

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:03.010
The southern Solomon Islands
...the territorial waters of Guadalcanal.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.180
Territorial waters?

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:15.860
New Guinea

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:15.810
Rabaul

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:15.810
Australia

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:15.860
Guadalcanal Island

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.600
Right now, in July of the 17th Showa Year...

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.150
...2500 combat engineers are in the process of building a force there.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:24.200
Rabaul

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:18.110
According to history, on the 7th of August,

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:21.570
18,000 US Marines will land on the island,

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.910
and take the airstrip by force.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:28.120
Afterwards, an intense battle broke out on land,

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:32.120
which resulted in the loss of more than 22,000 lives.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.120
The aim of this ship,

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:36.130
is to prevent the battle from happening,

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:40.260
...and rescue as many lives as possible, regardless of their race!

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.180
You mean we're going to...

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:45.220
...change history?!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.510
We will depart at 0600.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.390
I'd like to remind everyone aboard this ship...

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.440
...that we are not going to take sides.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:21:00.230
The operation must comply with the SDF weapons...

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.900
to be used with the intent of rescue...

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:05.200
...and not attack. That's all.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.450
Finally! Some action!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.790
It's time to show what we're made of!

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.170
I have no objections to the Captain's decision.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.920
What I need is to accomplish my mission.

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:28.640
The history we're writing isn't connected to our 21st Century.

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.140
Kusaka's words are like narcotics.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.600
Dangerous, yet sweet.

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:36.390
I'm just as lost myself.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:39.150
But, after coming this far...

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.610
...what other choice do we have left?

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:43.940
Captain! I will...

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.450
...I will support your decision, Captain!

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.580
Briefing Session next!

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:56.460
We need to come up with the best strategy for this operation!

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:57.540
Yes!

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.270
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.430 --> 00:22:22.500
Just peacefully

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:34.320
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:47.190
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:53.830
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:59.910
I kept on praying

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:11.720
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:27.400
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.970 --> 00:23:42.300
To Attack?!

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:43.760
Don't tell me, I have to shoot it down?!

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:45.390
Can you carry this burden?!

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:48.690
The responsibility of 100, even 1000 years of world history!

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:52.980
Indeed, this is going to change everything.

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:54.690
I'm an SDF officer.

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:58.360
I don't harbor any doubts about rescuing a life before me.

00:23:58.360 --> 00:24:01.240
We are now entering the Japanese-American war.

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:04.950
Next Episode: Interchange

00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:03.780
Well then, I'll see you at Guadalcanal.

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
